**MAJOR REVISION**

The note does not prove Theorem RAT in its stated generality. The interior coupling construction substantially closes the blind round’s finite-algebra gap, and WA is a valid transfer theorem. The remaining problems concern the claimed weight regularity, one-point moments, boundary normalization, parent filters, and composition. Several displayed assertions are false.

I found no counterexample to the intended DW-specific RAT inequalities with RAT-2’s displayed error term. The findings below are proof failures and overstatements, rather than an established FATAL counterexample to that intended theorem.

Locations refer to [c12rat_results.md](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/c12rat_results.md).

| # | Severity | Location | Finding | Suggested fix |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | MAJOR | §1.4, ADM | A fixed-exponent scaling law over the entire child filter range neglects accumulated saddle-point drift. The proof establishes substantially less than (Adm). | State local scaling and a separate global upper bound; retain the varying saddle point where needed. |
